# MC-B-F2. L §5.18 Partial answers: "A line marked partial prints, when its value is a hole, its known part and the
# named holes it is linear in, each with its coefficient: sums, differences ..."; L §5.19 (and §5.10 Balances): "a
# balance means ... before a place's first reading, its opening plus what is booked since". bal(w, 2025-12-31) =
# opening 100.00 DUK - the March spending (a hole; every other month 0.00): 100.00 DUK + -1 x the hole. accounts are
# signed (L §5.10), so no sign rule meets the hole. snap8 printed the plain hole.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
source s "s"
place w: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 2025-01-01..
input sp[m in months]: money DUK question "spent?"
version o
  cite s
  known 2025-01-01
  opening[w] = 100.00 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  sp[*] = 0.00 DUK "the other months"
  sp[2025-03] = ?"What was spent in March?" "March"
move spent[m in months]: transfers
  on end_of(m) - 1
  leg cash from w to shop amount sp[m]
ask q: bal(w, 2025-12-31) law 2025-12-31 partial
=== expect
q: 100.00 DUK + -1 × ?"What was spent in March?" (sp[2025-03])
  unfulfilled: spent[2025-03]
  law date 2025-12-31, cut 2026-01-01
